<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Eleazar López Contreras</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1883">1883</a>–<a href="/years/1973">1973</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Eleazar López Contreras was a Venezuelan army officer and politician who was president of Venezuela from 1935 to 1941. Minister of war under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/juan-vicente-gomez">Juan Vicente Gómez</a>, he succeeded the dictator on his death and began a cautious political opening, allowing greater freedom of the press and of organisation while keeping firm control, and handed power to his chosen successor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/isaias-medina-angarita">Isaías Medina Angarita</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/eleazar-lopez-contreras.jpg" alt="Eleazar López Contreras" width="320" height="404" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Eleazar_L%C3%B3pez_Contreras.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
